# Vectis Mail Server — Dovecot Master Users (Impersonation)
# Generated by config engine — do not edit manually
#
# NOTE (2.4 migration): this file is generated but NOT yet wired into dovecot.conf
# (no !include / compose mount) — it is scaffolding for the Phase 2D admin
# impersonation feature. It retains 2.3-era passdb syntax and MUST be migrated to
# Dovecot 2.4 (passdb dict {} form) and functionally validated before it is wired
# in. See [[project_dsar_retention_track]] / the dovecot 2.4 migration PR.
#
# Master users can access any mailbox via the "user*master" login format.
# Used by admin impersonation (Phase 2D.3) with temporary credentials
# stored in Valkey (30-minute TTL).
#
# Authentication flow:
#   1. Admin calls POST /api/v1/mailboxes/{id}/impersonate
#   2. API generates temp password, stores in Valkey as impersonate:user@domain*vectis-admin
#   3. Admin connects via IMAP as user@domain*vectis-admin with temp password
#   4. Dovecot passdb (dict driver) looks up the master user cred in Valkey
#   5. Credentials expire after 30 minutes (Valkey TTL)

# Master user passdb — checks Valkey for temporary impersonation credentials.
# The dict driver connects to Valkey and looks up the key.
passdb {
    driver = dict
    master = yes
    args = /etc/dovecot/dovecot-dict-master.conf.ext
    result_success = return-ok
    result_failure = continue
}
